invariant: INV-46
file: mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: mlkem.c guards its call to the vector inverse NTT on a macro no
  build defines, so a host object's sessions run mlkem_poly.c's inverse
  loops. Every vector passes, because the loops compute the same
  coefficients, so the script compiles mlkem.c as a host object does and
  requires it to call mlk_vector_invntt and not mlk_poly_invntt.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    mlk_vector_invntt(p);
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME_PATH
    mlk_vector_invntt(p);
